### =====================================================================
### appointMe - requests.http  (Days 5-12)
### Since Day 12 the tenant comes from the TOKEN, not from the URL.
###
### HOW TO RUN
###   1. Load scripts/dev-seed.sql (Alice, Bob, tenants 1-2, sample data).
###   2. Run L1 (login) and then SEL1 (select tenant 1). Both store {{token}}.
###   3. Everything under SERVICES / CUSTOMERS / APPOINTMENTS uses {{token}}.
###   4. The FOUNDER and BOB sections keep their OWN tokens, so they never
###      overwrite Alice's.
### Tokens last 30 minutes. Sudden 401s => run L1 and SEL1 again.
### "EXPECT" tells you the status you should see.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### --- Ids from dev-seed.sql -------------------------------------------
@serviceId = 1
@service2Id = 2
@otherServiceId = 3
@customerId = 1
@otherCustomerId = 3
@staffId = 2
@otherStaffId = 3


### ======================================================================
### AUTH  (Days 10-11)
### ======================================================================

### L1. LOGIN as Alice. EXPECT 200 with accessToken (a USER token, no tenant yet)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("userToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### L2. Wrong password. EXPECT 401 "Invalid email or password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "wrong-password" }

### L3. Unknown email. EXPECT 401, body IDENTICAL to L2 (apart from timestamp)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "whatever123" }

### L4. Email in other capitals. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  ALICE@TEST.COM ", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

### L5. Missing fields. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### R1. Password too short. EXPECT 400, errors.password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "short@example.com", "password": "abc", "fullName": "Shorty" }

### R2. Bad email + blank name. EXPECT 400, errors for email and fullName
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nope", "password": "correct-horse-1", "fullName": "" }


### ======================================================================
### TOKEN CHECKS  (Day 11)
### ======================================================================

### J1. Who am I? EXPECT 200, Alice
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### J2. No token. EXPECT 401 (JSON body, WWW-Authenticate: Bearer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/services

### J3. Garbage token. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer this.is.not-a-token

### J4. Wrong scheme (Basic). EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6cGFzcw==

### J5. Unsigned "alg":"none" token claiming to be user 1. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIn0.eyJzdWIiOiIxIn0.

### J6. TAMPERED token: paste a real token with one changed character. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE.TAMPERED.TOKEN.HERE


### ======================================================================
### TENANT CONTEXT  (Day 12)
### ======================================================================

### M1. Which businesses am I in? EXPECT 200, [ tenant 1 "Test Barber", role OWNER ]
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/memberships
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### M2. Business endpoint with a USER token (no tenant chosen yet).
###     EXPECT 403 "No business selected"
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### SEL1. Select tenant 1. EXPECT 200, accessToken + tenantId 1 + role OWNER.
###       Stores the TENANT token as {{token}}.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### SEL2. Alice is NOT a member of tenant 2. EXPECT 404 (not 403: don't confirm it exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/2
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### SEL3. Tenant that doesn't exist. EXPECT 404, same body as SEL2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### SEL4. Current business, read from the token. EXPECT 200, "Test Barber"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### SEL5. The old /tenants/{id} route is gone. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### SEL6. Old URL style no longer exists. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/1/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ======================================================================
### SERVICES  (tenant comes from {{token}})
### ======================================================================

### S1. Create. EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Shave", "durationMinutes": 20, "price": 12.50 }

### S2. Blank name. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "durationMinutes": 30, "price": 25.00 }

### S3. Negative duration. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": -5, "price": 25.00 }

### S4. Missing price. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": 30 }

### S5. List. EXPECT 200, ONLY tenant 1's services (Haircut, Beard Trim, + any you created)
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S6. Get one. EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S7. Missing service. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S8. Update. EXPECT 200, new price
PUT {{baseUrl}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": 30, "price": 28.00, "active": true }

### S9. Soft delete Beard Trim. EXPECT 204 (rerun dev-seed.sql to restore it)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/services/{{service2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ======================================================================
### CUSTOMERS
### ======================================================================

### C1. Create. EXPECT 201, email saved lowercase
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Cara Lee", "email": "Cara@Example.com", "phone": "6900000010" }

### C2. Duplicate email (other capitals). EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Another Ann", "email": "ANN@example.com" }

### C3. Blank name + bad email. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "", "email": "not-an-email" }

### C4. No email. EXPECT 201 (run twice: both succeed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Walk-in Customer" }

### C5. Search + page + sort. EXPECT 200, names containing "ann"
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?name=ann&page=0&size=10&sort=fullName,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C6. Size cap. EXPECT "size": 100
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?size=100000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C7. Bad sort field. EXPECT 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?sort=nonsense
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C8. Get one. EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C9. Update keeping the same email. EXPECT 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith-Jones", "email": "ann@example.com", "phone": "6900000099" }

### C10. Update to Ben's email. EXPECT 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith-Jones", "email": "ben@example.com" }


### ======================================================================
### APPOINTMENTS  (use dates in the FUTURE; today is 2026-10-20)
### ======================================================================

### A1. Create. EXPECT 201, endsAt = startsAt + 30 min (Haircut)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffId": {{staffId}},
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-10T09:00:00Z",
  "notes": "First visit"
}

### A1b. 15-minute service. EXPECT 201, endsAt = 10:15
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": 2, "serviceId": {{service2Id}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-10T10:00:00Z" }

### A2. In the past. EXPECT 400, errors.startsAt
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2020-01-01T09:00:00Z" }

### A3. Missing fields. EXPECT 400, several errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2026-11-10T11:00:00Z" }

### A4. ATTACK: staff member of another tenant. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{otherStaffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-10T11:00:00Z" }

### A5. ATTACK: customer of another tenant. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{otherCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-10T11:00:00Z" }

### A5b. ATTACK: service of another tenant. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{otherServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-10T11:00:00Z" }

### A6. Inactive service. EXPECT 400 (run S9 first, which deactivates service 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{service2Id}},
  "startsAt": "2026-11-10T12:00:00Z" }

### A7. List a range. EXPECT 200, sorted by startsAt
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A8. Range too big. EXPECT 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-31T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A9. from after to. EXPECT 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?from=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A10. Mark appointment 1 completed. EXPECT 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "COMPLETED" }

### A11. Change it again. EXPECT 409 (COMPLETED is final)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "NO_SHOW" }

### A12. Unknown status. EXPECT 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "BANANA" }


### ======================================================================
### ISOLATION as Alice (tenant 1 token). The URL can no longer name a tenant,
### so the only attack left is guessing OTHER tenants' record ids.
### ======================================================================

### ISO1. Tenant 2's service by id. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/{{otherServiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ISO2. Update tenant 2's service. EXPECT 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/services/{{otherServiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hacked", "durationMinutes": 1, "price": 0.00, "active": true }

### ISO3. Delete tenant 2's service. EXPECT 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/services/{{otherServiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ISO4. Tenant 2's customer. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{otherCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ISO5. A "tenantId" inside the body is IGNORED (the DTO has no such field).
###       EXPECT 201, and the service appears in tenant 1's list, NOT tenant 2's
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": 2, "name": "Smuggled", "durationMinutes": 10, "price": 1.00 }


### ======================================================================
### FOUNDER FLOW: register, create a business, become its OWNER.
### Uses {{founderToken}} so Alice's {{token}} is untouched.
### ======================================================================

### F1. Register. EXPECT 201 (rerun gives 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "founder@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1", "fullName": "Fay Founder" }

### F2. Login. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "founder@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("founderToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### F3. Create a business. EXPECT 201 (rerun gives 409: slug taken). Stores its id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Fresh Salon", "slug": "fresh-salon", "timezone": "Europe/Athens" }

> {%
    client.global.set("newTenantId", response.body.id);
%}

### F4. Memberships. EXPECT 200, the new business with role OWNER
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/memberships
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}

### F5. Select the new business. EXPECT 200, role OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/{{newTenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("founderToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### F6. Current business. EXPECT 200 "Fresh Salon"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/current
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}

### F7. A brand-new business has no data. EXPECT 200, []
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}

### F8. Create a service in the new business. EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Blow dry", "durationMinutes": 40, "price": 20.00 }

### F9. Duplicate slug. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Copy", "slug": "fresh-salon", "timezone": "UTC" }

### F10. Unknown time zone. EXPECT 400 "Unknown time zone"
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mars Barber", "slug": "mars-barber", "timezone": "Mars/Base" }

### F11. Bad slug. EXPECT 400, errors.slug
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{founderToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bad Slug", "slug": "Test Barber", "timezone": "UTC" }


### ======================================================================
### BOB FLOW: one person, two businesses (STAFF in tenant 1 AND tenant 2).
### Uses {{bobToken}}.
### ======================================================================

### B1. Login as Bob. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("bobUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("bobToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### B2. Memberships. EXPECT 200, TWO entries (tenant 1 STAFF, tenant 2 STAFF)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/memberships
Authorization: Bearer {{bobUserToken}}

### B3. Select tenant 2 (Second Gym). EXPECT 200, role STAFF
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/2
Authorization: Bearer {{bobUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("bobToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### B4. Services. EXPECT 200, ONLY "Yoga Class" (tenant 2's)
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### B5. Tenant 1's service by id. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### B6. Customers. EXPECT 200, ONLY "Zoe Gym"
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### B7. Tenant 1's appointment 1 (run A1 first). EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### B8. Switch to tenant 1. EXPECT 200, role STAFF
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bobUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("bobToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### B9. Services again. EXPECT 200, tenant 1's services (Haircut, Beard Trim...)
GET {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
